theorem uo_add (l : ℕ) (x y : ℕ → R) : Uo l (x + y) = Uo l x + Uo l y := rfl

/- English proof (translation)
Establish an intermediate fact. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Normalize the expressions using the abelian group laws. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Normalize the expressions using the abelian group laws.
-/
theorem uo_mul_dep (l : ℕ) (hl : 0 < l) (a b : ℕ → R) :
    Uo l (mul (dep l a) (dep l b)) = Uo l (mul a b) - mul (Uo l a) (Uo l b) := by
  have e : Uo l (mul a b) = Uo l (mul (dep l a) (dep l b)) + mul (Uo l a) (Uo l b) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [dep_add l hl a, dep_add l hl b]
    rw [mul_add_left', mul_add_right', mul_add_right', uo_add, uo_add, uo_add,
      uo_mul_vo l hl, uo_dep, zero_mul', mul_comm' (Vo l (Uo l a)) (dep l b), uo_mul_vo l hl, uo_dep,
      zero_mul', uo_mul_vo l hl, uo_vo l hl]
    abel
  rw [e]; abel

/- English proof (translation)
Apply function extensionality and compare values at an arbitrary argument. Simplify using the standard rewrite rules. Consider separately whether the proposition holds or fails. Extract witnesses or component facts from the available result. Separate the alternatives or extract the components of the hypothesis.

